cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "orbital-thermal: a reduced-order orbital data-center radiator model"
abstract: >-
  An audit-closed Python package for reduced-order orbital data-center radiator
  modeling. It implements the analytic thermodynamic bounds of the companion
  preprints as executable functions and extends them to time-dependent,
  environment-coupled behavior (an orbit-varying effective sink and a one-node
  transient solver with a convergence certificate). Its headline result is an
  exact-view-factor correction to a public radiator model. The package supports
  mathematical, software, and cross-model verification; it is not validated
  against flown hardware.
type: software
authors:
